GJS OSK by Vishram1123
https://extensions.gnome.org/extension/5949/gjs-osk/

My Review: One of the worst things about Gnome's touchscreen functionality is how awful
the OSK can be. Sometimes it works fine, other times it's weird and jumpy and starts
having characters dissapear. Not to mention how often you'll click on an area to type
and then the keyboard comes infront of the text box, covering your view entirely. So
an alternative was very much necessary and this extention is the only one that seems 
to be compatible. It's a much needed improvement, huge benefit is how you can move the
keyboard around so you dont have to worry about it covering up your text. The app itself
is quite customizeable and lets you create your own keyboard from scratch by editing the 
json file. The default layouts aren't amazing for the tablet format to be honest so I 
made my own after a lot of trail and error to a layout that feels a lot more natural (to
me at least). You can find my custom format within the "Better OSK" folder with my settings.

Developer's Description:
A new Onscreen Keyboard built using GNOME JS
